WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.375
Your plan says the website launches on the sixteenth of October.

00:00:04.495 --> 00:00:08.845
But it's October second, and the work isn't going quite as planned.

00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:11.465
So when will you really launch?

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:18.190
In PlantUML Ultimate, turn on Progress forecast and pick a status date.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:27.910
The app looks at how much of each task is complete, works out what's left, and projects the whole plan forward, respecting your dependencies and your closed weekends.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.535
And there's the answer.

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:34.980
Projected finish: October twenty-first.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.100
Three working days later than planned.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:46.345
On the chart, the grey bar is the plan, the blue bar is the forecast, and the hatching marks work that's running past its planned finish.

00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:50.070
But a number isn't enough.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.190
You need to know why.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:59.510
Click Backend, and the inspector explains it: planned to finish on October ninth, forecast to finish on the fourteenth.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:03.955
It's only ten percent done, with nine working days remaining.

00:01:05.455 --> 00:01:09.455
Zoom out, and the project finish causes tell you where to act.

00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:13.125
One root task is moving the release: Backend.

00:01:13.245 --> 00:01:17.045
It holds up two linked tasks, and the Launch milestone.

00:01:17.165 --> 00:01:19.690
Everything else is on plan.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.315
Now try a what-if.

00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:27.110
Suppose Backend only needs six more working days.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.505
Type it in, and the projected finish snaps back to the sixteenth.

00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:33.700
Plus zero days.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.695
Your source file hasn't changed, so it's safe to explore.

00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:42.220
When the delay is real, you can accept it.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:49.565
Apply to plan shows exactly which tasks will change: Backend gets longer, Integration and Launch move with it.

00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:54.060
Review the changes, apply them, and the plan now matches reality.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.385
Know where you really stand, see why, and test your options.

00:01:59.505 --> 00:02:03.130
Progress forecast, in PlantUML Ultimate.
